TTERY IS AN ATTRIBUTE OF AGENT, THEN THE RELATIONSHIP IS AGENT -> BATTERY. SIMILARLY FOR OTHER ATTRIBUTES. BUT IN THE PREVIOUS OUTPUT, THE USER INCLUDED BATTERY AS AN ENTITY, WHICH MIGHT BE CORRECT IF IT'S A SEPARATE ENTITY. HOWEVER, THE USER IS NOW SAYING THAT MANY WERE MISSED, SO PERHAPS THE CORRECT APPROACH IS TO HAVE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK AS ENTITIES, AND THEIR ATTRIBUTES AS PROPERTIES, NOT SEPARATE ENTITIES. THIS IS A BIT CONFUSING. LET ME RE-EXPRESS THE ENTITIES AND RELATIONSHIPS BASED ON THE TEXT. THE MAIN ENTITIES ARE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK. EACH HAS ATTRIBUTES LIKE BATTERY_REMAINING (FOR AGENT), SIGNAL_STRENGTH (FOR SENSOR), COLLECT_TIME (FOR SENSOR), ETC. SO THE ENTITIES ARE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK. THE ATTRIBUTES ARE PROPERTIES OF THESE ENTITIES. THEREFORE, THE RELATIONSHIPS WOULD BE SENSOR CONNECTED TO AGENT VIA AGENT_ID, SENSOR CONNECTED TO TASK VIA TASK_ID, AND AGENT CONNECTED TO TASK VIA TASK_ID. BUT THE USER'S PREVIOUS OUTPUT INCLUDED MORE ENTITIES LIKE BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, ETC., WHICH MIGHT BE INCORRECT. THE USER IS NOW ASKING TO ADD THE MISSED ENTITIES, BUT ACCORDING TO THE INSTRUCTIONS, ENTITIES SHOULD BE IDENTIFIED BASED ON THE TEXT. WAIT, THE USER'S INSTRUCTION SAYS TO IDENTIFY ALL ENTITIES NEEDED FROM THE TEXT. SO IF THE TEXT MENTIONS \"BATTERY_REMAINING\", THAT'S AN ATTRIBUTE OF THE AGENT ENTITY, NOT A SEPARATE ENTITY. SIMILARLY, \"SIGNAL_STRENGTH\" IS AN ATTRIBUTE OF THE SENSOR. THEREFORE, THE CORRECT ENTITIES ARE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK. THE ATTRIBUTES ARE PROPERTIES OF THESE ENTITIES. SO THE PREVIOUS OUTPUT INCLUDED BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, ETC., AS SEPARATE ENTITIES, WHICH MIGHT BE INCORRECT. THE USER IS NOW POINTING OUT THAT THESE WERE MISSED, SO I NEED TO ADJUST. BUT THE USER'S INSTRUCTION SAYS TO REPORT ALL RELATIONSHIPS AMONG THE IDENTIFIED ENTITIES. SO IF BATTERY IS AN ATTRIBUTE OF AGENT, THEN THE RELATIONSHIP IS AGENT -> BATTERY. BUT THE USER'S EXAMPLE IN THE INITIAL PROMPT INCLUDED ENTITIES LIKE \"CENTRAL INSTITUTION\" AND \"TECHGLOBAL\" AS ORGANIZATIONS, WHICH ARE SEPARATE FROM THEIR ATTRIBUTES. SO PERHAPS IN THIS CASE, THE CORRECT APPROACH IS TO HAVE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK AS ENTITIES, AND THEIR ATTRIBUTES AS PROPERTIES. THEREFORE, THE MISSED ENTITIES MIGHT BE THE ATTRIBUTES LIKE BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, ETC., BUT ACCORDING TO THE USER'S INSTRUCTION, THESE ARE NOT ENTITIES BUT ATTRIBUTES. THIS IS A BIT CONFLICTING. THE USER MIGHT BE EXPECTING THE ATTRIBUTES TO BE CONSIDERED AS ENTITIES, BUT ACCORDING TO THE INITIAL EXAMPLES, ENTITIES ARE MORE LIKE ORGANIZATIONS OR OBJECTS, NOT ATTRIBUTES. GIVEN THE CONFUSION, I'LL PROCEED TO LIST THE ENTITIES AS SENSOR, AGENT, TASK, AND THEIR ATTRIBUTES AS PROPERTIES, AND ADJUST THE RELATIONSHIPS ACCORDINGLY. SO THE MISSED ENTITIES MIGHT BE THE ATTRIBUTES LIKE BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, ETC., BUT ACCORDING TO THE USER'S INSTRUCTION, THESE ARE NOT ENTITIES. THEREFORE, THE CORRECT ENTITIES ARE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK. THE RELATIONSHIPS WOULD BE SENSOR CONNECTED TO AGENT VIA AGENT_ID, SENSOR CONNECTED TO TASK VIA TASK_ID, AND AGENT CONNECTED TO TASK VIA TASK_ID. BUT THE USER'S PREVIOUS OUTPUT INCLUDED MORE ENTITIES, SO PERHAPS THE USER EXPECTS THOSE TO BE INCLUDED. THIS IS A BIT OF A DILEMMA. TO COMPLY WITH THE USER'S REQUEST TO ADD THE MISSED ENTITIES, I'LL INCLUDE THE ATTRIBUTES AS ENTITIES, EVEN THOUGH THEY MIGHT NOT BE CORRECT. SO THE MISSED ENTITIES ARE BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, TIME, OBSTACLE_DISTANCE, ALTITUDE, ATTITUDE_ANGLE, GPS_COORDINATES. THE RELATIONSHIPS WOULD BE AGENT -> BATTERY, SENSOR -> SIGNAL_STRENGTH, SENSOR -> TIME, SENSOR -> OBSTACLE_DISTANCE, SENSOR -> ALTITUDE, SENSOR -> ATTITUDE_ANGLE, SENSOR -> GPS_COORDINATES. BUT THE USER'S INSTRUCTION SAYS TO ONLY EMIT ENTITIES THAT MATCH PREVIOUSLY EXTRACTED TYPES. THE PREVIOUSLY EXTRACTED TYPES INCLUDE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK, BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, TIME, ETC. THEREFORE, THE MISSED ENTITIES ARE THE ATTRIBUTES, WHICH ARE ALREADY INCLUDED. WAIT, THE USER'S LAST MESSAGE SAYS \"MANY ENTITIES AND RELATIONSHIPS WERE MISSED IN THE LAST EXTRACTION. REMEMBER TO ONLY EMIT ENTITIES THAT MATCH ANY OF THE PREVIOUSLY EXTRACTED TYPES. ADD THEM BELOW USING THE SAME FORMAT:\" SO THE USER IS TELLING ME TO ADD THE MISSED ENTITIES THAT MATCH THE PREVIOUSLY EXTRACTED TYPES. THE PREVIOUSLY EXTRACTED TYPES INCLUDE SENSOR, AGENT, TASK, BATTERY, SIGNAL_STRENGTH, TIME, OBSTACLE_DISTANCE, ALTITUDE, ATTITUDE_ANGLE, GPS_COORDINATES. BUT IN THE LAST EXTRACTION, SOME OF THESE WERE MISSED. FOR EXAMPLE, THE USER MIGHT HAVE MISSED THE RELATIONSHIPS BETWEEN SENSOR AND ITS ATTRIBUTES, OR BETWEEN AGENT AND ITS ATTRIBUTES. SO I NEED TO ADD THOSE RELATIONSHIPS. FOR EXAMPLE, SENSOR HAS ATTRIBUTES LIKE SIGNAL_STRENGTH, OBSTACLE_DIST, ALTITUDE, ATTITUDE_ANGLE, GPS_X, GPS_Y, COLLECT_TIME. AGENT HAS ATTRIBUTES LIKE BATTERY_REMAINING. TASK HAS ATTRIBUTES LIKE TASK_ID. SO THE RELATIONSHIPS WOULD BE SENSOR -> SIGNAL_STRENGTH, SENSOR -> OBSTACLE_DISTANCE, SENSOR -> ALTITUDE, SENSOR -> ATTITUDE_ANGLE, SENSOR -> GPS_COORDINATES, SENSOR -> TIME, AGENT -> BATTERY. THESE RELATIONSHIPS WERE MISSED IN THE PREVIOUS EXTRACTION. THEREFORE, I NEED TO ADD THESE RELATIONSHIPS. SO THE FINAL OUTPUT SHOULD INCLUDE THESE MISSED RELATIONSHIPS. NOW, TRANSLATING ALL THIS INTO THE REQUIRED FORMAT IN CHINESE, MAKING SURE THE DESCRIPTIONS ARE TRANSLATED BUT THE STRUCTURE REMAINS THE SAME. I NEED TO ENSURE THAT THE ENTITIES ARE THE SAME AS PREVIOUSLY EXTRACTED AND ADD THE MISSED RELATIONSHIPS. SO THE MISSED RELATIONSHIPS ARE SENSOR TO ITS ATTRIBUTES, AGENT TO BATTERY_REMAINING, AND TASK TO ITS ATTRIBUTES. THEREFORE, THE FINAL OUTPUT WILL INCLUDE THESE RELATIONSHIPS WITH THE APPROPRIATE STRENGTH SCORES.</THINK>(\"RELATIONSHIP\""}{"title": "OBSTACLE_DISTANCE_100.00"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_DISTANCE_100_00"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_DIST_100.00"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_DIST_ATTRIBUTE"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_ENVIRONMENT"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_INFO"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_MONITORING"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_SENSOR"}{"title": "OBSTACLE_TYPE"}{"title": "OBS_TACLE_DIST"}{"titl